# Platform backlog — 2.7.0

Updated 2026-09-07. This is the authoritative outstanding-work list. Reconciled
against the active server, configuration, API handlers, release notes and
qualification records. Checked means implemented, not deployed or independently
certified. Historical review findings remain in CODEX_TODO.md. Older milestone
plans are design proposals, not current completion checklists.

## Production qualification and operations

- [x] Run hosted release CI; require qualify, scanners and container on up-to-date main, including administrators. Configuration is recorded in .github/branch-protection.json.
- [ ] Qualify the actual OAuth identity provider with valid, insufficient-scope and revoked tokens using mailhub-authcheck.
- [ ] Qualify production Object Lock storage, access separation, retention, encryption and recovery; preserve independent receipts/checkpoints.
- [ ] Configure and test provider-specific fencing, independent verification, standby activation, readiness and traffic switching. Measure RPO/RTO.
- [ ] Provision production domains, MX/SPF/DKIM/DMARC records, TLS certificates, API secrets and connector trust; verify DKIM/ARC interoperability with actual DNS/keys.
- [ ] Review monitor-mode SPF/DMARC policies and opt into enforcement after traffic validation; decide whether greylisting is appropriate.
- [ ] Review Rspamd task-timeout warnings and scanner budgets under production traffic; verify required-scanner outage behavior.
- [ ] Configure production directory/recipient lookup and test aliases, disabled users and directory outages.
- [ ] Install Prometheus rules, alert routing and the dedicated mailflow probe; exercise alerts and create Grafana dashboards.
- [ ] Run representative sustained load, disk-full, crash, network-loss and recovery drills; tune workers, quotas, DNS and destination limits from measurements. The old 1,000–5,000 msg/s target is unqualified.
- [ ] Migrate existing installations' file ownership/permissions; new journal/tier files use 0600 and directories use 0700.
- [ ] Establish and exercise retention/disposal schedules for DLQ, tracked DSNs, audit logs, backups and exported evidence; configure encrypted storage and key recovery in the deployment.

See docs/DEPLOYMENT_QUALIFICATION.md for recorded local evidence and remaining
external gates. No production rollout is implied by the implementation checklist.

## Engineering gaps and deferred enhancements

- [x] Add gemsads-conf validated file editing, SQLite maintenance and relay probes; repair adsemailadm real API behavior and remove fabricated results. See docs/CLI_ADMINISTRATION.md.
- [ ] Implement general queued-message hold/release, full deferred-queue flush and requeue if required; current queue CLI is not full Postfix parity.

- [x] Align mailbox API password validation with bcrypt’s 72-byte limit; oversized create/update requests fail before persistence.
- [x] Reject unknown YAML fields and extra documents; provide `--check-config` without startup side effects.

- [x] Integrate replicated-volume active/passive ownership checks, DRBD quorum/mount verification and failover deployment templates. See docs/HIGH_AVAILABILITY.md; real cluster/fencing qualification remains operational.
- [ ] Implement active-active mailbox/shard ownership if required; current HA uses a single owner per replicated volume.
- [x] Implement persistent IMAP folder mutations, metadata APPEND/COPY, flags, decoded search, protocol notifications and restored-service acceptance checks.
- [x] Correct active Sieve validation, failure handling, MIME body matching and persistent routing/flags; reject unsupported programs explicitly.
- [x] Fix post-merge review defects: Sieve any-flag matching, space-separated flag operations, strict condition separators, and account-wide JMAP mailbox state; add regressions including local delivery.
- [x] Replace fabricated JMAP reads/write success with durable owner-scoped reads/downloads and explicit unsupported-operation errors.
- [x] Complete Sieve flag compatibility: delivery :flags, named flag sets, hasflag match types/comparators, snapshot semantics and stored-delivery regressions. See docs/SIEVE_FLAGS.md.
- [x] Fix shared IMAP notification responses; qualify three simultaneous sessions, IDLE flag delivery, silent STORE, expunge fan-out and account isolation over TLS.
- [x] Cancel notification waits after logout; add concurrent APPEND/STORE and abrupt-IDLE reconnect regressions, live evidence reports and a preliminary UAT sign-off template.
- [x] Implement transactional IMAP MOVE/UID MOVE, preserve metadata without extra quota usage, reject read-only moves, notify source/destination sessions and verify restored moved mail.
- [ ] Execute the named desktop/mobile client acceptance rows in docs/PRELIMINARY_UAT.md and record candidate evidence and operator sign-off.
- [x] Implement JMAP keyword updates with conditional state checks and durable paginated Email/changes, including SMTP/IMAP changes, bounded history and restored-service regressions.
- [x] Correct JMAP method-call/response wire encoding to standard invocation arrays and include the real HTTP endpoint in release qualification.
- [x] Add stable mailbox identities, JMAP Mailbox/set and durable Mailbox/changes, with rename/reparent, subscription, empty deletion protection and restored-service qualification.
- [x] Add JMAP email move and destruction with atomic keyword/membership updates, owner/state checks, IMAP notifications and durable change-feed restore coverage.
- [x] Add owner-scoped bounded uploads and atomic Email/import, with expiry/eviction, quota/state protection, raw MIME preservation, IMAP arrival and backup/restore coverage.
- [x] Add bounded structured Email/set creation and authenticated EmailSubmission/set/get with primary Identity/get, shared SMTP admission, durable acceptance receipts, MIME/Bcc privacy and restore qualification.
- [x] Add JMAP submission success email updates/destruction, durable email/receipt query synchronization, paginated receipt changes and owner-scoped receipt deletion, including restore qualification.
- [x] Implement documented Sieve gaps: redirect, vacation, copy and multiple delivery actions with durable execution plans, retry checkpoints, loop limits and vacation suppression across restore.
- [x] Add Email/query and EmailSubmission/query anchors, signed offsets and negative positions, with filtered/owner-scoped lookup and unchanged query snapshots across pages.
- [x] Add bounded JMAP bodyStructure composition/readback, inline CID parts and owner-scoped MIME-part blob reuse, with independent copied bytes and restored-service qualification.
- [x] Add bounded JMAP delayed submission and atomic cancellation, with durable pending/final/canceled receipt changes and restored pending-send qualification.
- [x] Add immutable JMAP thread grouping, Thread/get/changes, collapsed queries and bounded authenticated SSE push. See docs/JMAP_THREADS_PUSH.md.
- [x] Add opt-in automatic receipt/Sieve journal checkpoint retention, protecting pending sends, live retry sources and unexpired vacation intervals. Legacy unlinked checkpoints and mailbox tombstones remain retained. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
- [x] Reconcile M3: add provisioned-account LDAP/AD password authentication, scoped durable SCIM Users provisioning, and audience-bound JMAP tokens for a SAML identity broker. Native SAML browser endpoints and SMTP/IMAP OAuth are not claimed; provider qualification remains operational. See docs/ENTERPRISE_IDENTITY.md.
- [ ] Decide scope for trained AI spam models, phishing/learning pipelines and shared cluster reputation/outbreak state from M4–M6. Current mailstorm baselines are deterministic and per instance.
- [x] Implement durable daily DMARC XML aggregation, verified external mailto destinations, outbound delivery and administrative export/retry APIs. See docs/DMARC_REPORTING.md.
- [x] Expose actual listener security/DNS/greylisting statistics through scoped active REST routes. See docs/OPERATIONS_STATISTICS.md.
- [x] Add docs/openapi.json for the active management API, with CI checks for document structure/references, routes, permissions, JSON field drift and representative handler responses.
- [x] Add validated SIGHUP/API configuration reload through graceful process replacement, with read-only preflight and explicit reconnect/runtime-dependency boundaries. See docs/CONFIGURATION_RELOAD.md.
- [x] Measure and optimize storage header reads, metadata-only listings and bounded/coalesced DNS negative caching. Compression and speculative prefetch were evaluated as deferred alternatives, not silently enabled. See docs/PERFORMANCE_MEASUREMENTS.md.
- [x] Add offline personal-data inventory/export and staged local deletion, with shared/evidence protection, database cleanup, and explicit external log/backup/disposition obligations. Final request closure requires those obligations to be verified. See docs/PERSONAL_DATA.md.
- [x] Add TLS gRPC management, a scoped web console, durable signed management webhooks, bounded external admission plugins and sender/suffix transport routing. See docs/EXTENSIONS_ADMINISTRATION.md for supported contracts.
- [x] Harden submission defaults, reject unsafe relay/listener settings and prevent storage/HA changes through reload. See docs/CONFIGURATION_SAFETY.md.
- [x] Audit historical feature claims and inactive prototypes; archive the unfinished OAuth web-session prototype and document all remaining scope in docs/PROJECT_COMPLETION_AUDIT.md.

